6	 * StreetHubSupport, the fresh authored support group for the 2026-10-15 edition.
7	 *
8	 * The San Antonio world around the flood station and the places its warning goes. A wet asphalt
9	 * street with a hand-cut limestone curb and a dark gutter, a St. Augustine lawn with dormant brown
10	 * patches, a chain link fence whose second post carries an orange ankle-high paint band and a
11	 * swinging orange flagging tag, a live oak edge with low spreading limbs and grey ball moss, and the
12	 * corner of a painted bungalow porch with two steps and a rail where a worn phone lies screen up.
13	 *
14	 * FLOOD WATER IS FINISHED WATER. It is a surface, never a fill: the pale storm sky reflected near
15	 * its far edge, muddy brown under it, the mirrored posts, boots and lamps standing in it broken by
16	 * drifting ripple bands, a foam line along the far edge, a bright meniscus and a dark wet halo
17	 * along a spreading near edge, and drifting leaves and foam.
18	 *
19	 * The places the warning goes: a far cell tower; a distant, dark, windowless server building that
20	 * nothing reaches; a long street of bungalows that ends at the hub; a low limestone hub building
21	 * whose rooftop mast lamp and window light when a signal lands; the hub desk with a complete
22	 * seated responder (articulated shoulder, elbow, wrist and fingers, a head that turns to the
23	 * screen) and a flood path map of creek, streets, blocks and low points; a curb notice board
24	 * holding the validation card and the blank field result card; the paper street map with its
25	 * blank pin holes; and the curb folding table with a technician, a printed deployment plan and the
26	 * prototype's hard carry case with its front pocket and latch.
27	 *
28	 * Light matches the hero: low warm storm light from the upper left, cool fill from the right, long
29	 * soft shadows falling right. Nothing is symmetric. No logos, names, real streets, addresses,
30	 * agencies or measured values; the only figure drawn is the university's own reported validation
31	 * accuracy, passed in by the episode from its claim. People share one shape language: the same head
32	 * geometry for everyone, skin a fill that never changes the line work.
33	 *
34	 * Pure function of its props; the episode drives every prop from the film frame clock.
35	 */
